  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA mostly sunny and milder day is in store ahead of an \napproaching cold front. High temperatures will reach the 60s to\naround 70 which will be around 10 degrees above normal. While \nthe best forcing will remain north of the area, a passing cold \nfront should contain enough moisture to bring some light rain \nshowers tonight with the higher probabilities north and west of \nAlbany. Latest CAMs still suggest some isolated light showers or\nsprinkles could extend as far east as the Capital District so \nintroduced slight chance PoPs (15-25%) into these areas. \nMeasurable rainfall is favored for areas north and west of \nAlbany but will likely remain below 0.10 inches. For most areas,\nit has been nearly 2 weeks since measurable rainfall last \noccurred. Behind the front, drier and breezy conditions develop \non Friday with westerly winds gusting 20 to 30 mph with \nlocalized gusts to 35 mph into portions of the Capital District \nand Berkshires.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure rebuilds across the region for this weekend with\ndry and near seasonable weather with light winds. The high\nshifts to the east early next week allowing for temperatures to\nrun about 5 degrees above normal but mostly dry weather looks \nto continue. Thereafter, considerable uncertainty still exists \nwhen the next best chance for more widespread rainfall occurs. \nWill run with chance PoPs beginning next Wednesday until \nconfidence in the overall synoptic pattern improves.",
